			"widgets_values":[
				"subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the adult woman in <Picture 1>. Preserve her face, dark updo with loose curls beside her cheeks, coral-pink one-shoulder chiffon dress with a shoulder bow, earrings, necklace, and wristwatch. <Picture 1> is a character reference, not the opening frame. The video introduces one slender, straight silver practice sword with a simple dark handle.\n\nsummary:\nreference generation — A 10-second, 16:9 cinematic scene of <Subject 1> practicing sword forms in a bright bamboo grove while pink blossoms fall.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1>: fully_preserved — identity, hairstyle, dress, and visible accessories remain consistent.\n<Picture 1>: partially_preserved — use the woman’s appearance; do not reproduce the white studio background or multi-view layout.\n\ndetailed_description:\nA luminous spring morning. Tall green bamboo forms a layered background, and sunlight filters between the stems onto a clear patch of level stone. A flowering tree at the grove’s edge supplies the pale pink petals drifting through the scene. The atmosphere is fresh and bright, with natural skin texture, vivid but believable color, and soft depth in the background.\n\n[Shot 1] One continuous shot, with no cuts. <Subject 1> stands barefoot on the dry stone, holding the single practice sword in her right hand. Begin in a medium-wide three-quarter view that shows her face, full figure, and the complete blade. Her stance is poised and relaxed; the sword points diagonally down, and her left hand remains free. The camera glides slowly forward, then begins a smooth arc around her left side.\n\nDuring the first three seconds, she takes one measured step and raises the blade into a ready position. From seconds three to seven, she performs a connected sequence of precise practice movements: one level sweep, a controlled change of grip angle, and one rising diagonal cut. She pivots once to carry the movement through, keeping her balance on the stone. The blade follows a clear, continuous path; her hands maintain a stable hold. Her shoulder drape and loose curls respond lightly to the turn and the breeze.\n\nDuring the final three seconds, the camera completes its arc to a three-quarter front view and rises slightly. She finishes with the sword extended diagonally upward, then settles into a still, balanced stance. A cluster of petals passes through the sunlight in front of and behind her, while several fall to the stone. She lifts her gaze along the blade and holds a calm, focused expression. Keep the woman and sword unobstructed, preserve her facial features and outfit, and maintain one continuous camera path and natural motion throughout. No opponent, additional sword, scene change, or visible text.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nBamboo leaves rustling in a light breeze, distant morning birds, soft barefoot steps on stone, and distinct but restrained sword swishes. No dialogue.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nDelicate plucked strings and a soft flute melody support the graceful rhythm of the practice without overpowering the natural sounds."
